{"seq":4,"slug":"urban-and-sustainability","title":"城市与可持续建筑","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/urban-and-sustainability","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"urban-design-and-form","title":"城市设计与城市形态","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/urban-and-sustainability/urban-design-and-form","wordCount":1494,"readingTime":6},{"seq":2,"slug":"green-and-sustainable-design","title":"绿色建筑与可持续设计","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/urban-and-sustainability/green-and-sustainable-design","wordCount":1540,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"architecture-society-and-future","title":"建筑、社会与未来","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/urban-and-sustainability/architecture-society-and-future","wordCount":1534,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"城市与可持续建筑\">城市与可持续建筑</h1><p>单体建筑从不孤立存在，它嵌在街道、街区与城市的网络里；而在气候危机的当下，建筑业作为全球碳排放的最大来源之一，正承担着前所未有的生态责任。本章把视野从一栋楼扩展到一座城，再延伸到地球的尺度。</p>\n<p>本章分三课。第一课讲城市设计与城市形态，理解街道、广场与肌理如何塑造城市生活；第二课讲绿色建筑与可持续设计，介绍被动式策略、能耗与认证体系；第三课讲建筑与社会、未来趋势，思考建筑师的公共责任与数字时代的新可能。</p>\n"}